s really  fun going all over the country and  seeing the different solutions that  farmers have i think one of the  important things that we need to do is  also support them support them in both  the education and in the finance for  doing some of these solutions because  they are the custodians of lots of the  land that we have here in the uk and we  need to be supporting them because we  are also their customers and we really  want to buy food that is being  sustainably made and so we can all be  playing our part alongside them to help  deliver these nature-based solutions for  the land that we call home here in the  uk uh very briefly do you sometimes feel  like you're painted as the bad guys you  know agriculture responsible for lots of  methane emissions very briefly does that  feel like it do you look  too often agriculture seems the problem  whereas i see it as absolutely part of  the solution to biodiversity to carbon  but also to producing fantastic food in  a fantastic landscape okay stuart  roberts laura young really good to talk  to you both thanks very much for joining  us this evening
 

